=== man pages
LS(1)                         wbsh Manual                          LS(1)

NAME
       ls - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
       ls [OPTION]... [FILE]...

DESCRIPTION
       ls is built into wbsh and runs without an external program.

SEE ALSO
       wbsh(1), apropos(1)

wbsh                                                               LS(1)
CD(1)                         wbsh Manual                          CD(1)

NAME
       cd - change the shell working directory

SYNOPSIS
       cd [-L|[-P [-e]]] [DIR]

DESCRIPTION
       cd is a shell builtin. It behaves as the bash builtin of the same
       name, which bash(1) documents in full.

SEE ALSO
       bash(1), help(1)

wbsh                                                               CD(1)
CHOWN(1)                      wbsh Manual                       CHOWN(1)

NAME
       chown - change file owner and group
WBSH(1)                       wbsh Manual                        WBSH(1)

NAME
       wbsh - a bash-compatible shell for Windows

SYNOPSIS
       wbsh [OPTION]... [SCRIPT [ARG]...]
       wbsh -c COMMAND [ARG]...

